  "clarifyingQuestions": [
    "Does stderr imply failure or only exit code?",
    "Should logs be truncated?",
    "Which secret patterns should be redacted?",
    "Should command duration be included?"
  ],
  "followUps": [
    "Classify failures into test, lint, dependency, timeout, and infrastructure.",
    "Add log truncation with head and tail preservation.",
    "Attach command summaries to run timelines."
  ],
  "followUpGuide": [
    "For failure classes, inspect command name plus exit signal and known error fragments.",
    "",
    "For truncation, redact before retaining the first N and last N lines, avoid duplicating overlaps in short logs, and mark omitted content. A bounded line count still permits an arbitrarily long line; add a character or byte cap too.",
    "",
    "For timelines, emit a compact event per command and store raw logs separately with retention controls."
  ],
  "complexityAnalysis": [
    "- Scanning events and logs. Time: O(e + L), for e events and L captured characters. Space: O(B + k) for B returned characters and k returned lines, plus O(longest stream) temporary splitting storage. Count captured string contents as well as returned line entries.",
    "- Redaction is linear in each log line length. Space: O(line length) per processed line.",
    "- Classification follow-up: a fixed set of command-field checks can be O(1) per command, but scanning error fragments adds time proportional to the inspected text."
  ],
  "solutionGuide": [
    "Treat exit code as source of truth. Split each stream into lines, then apply the specified token redaction to each line. Preserve command fields and input events.",
    "",
    "```python",
    "import re",
    "",
    "",
    "def _redact(line: str) -> str:",
    "    return re.sub(r\"sk-[A-Za-z0-9_-]+\", \"[REDACTED]\", line)",
    "",
    "",
    "def classify_command_log(events: list[dict]) -> dict:",
    "    failed = 0",
    "    first_failure = None",
    "    redacted_logs = []",
    "    for event in events:",
    "        if event.get(\"exit_code\", 0) != 0:",
    "            failed += 1",
    "            if first_failure is None:",
    "                first_failure = event.get(\"cmd\")",
    "        for stream in (\"stdout\", \"stderr\"):",
    "            for line in str(event.get(stream) or \"\").splitlines():",
    "                redacted_logs.append(f\"{stream}: {_redact(line)}\")",
    "    return {",
    "        \"status\": \"failed\" if failed else \"passed\",",
    "        \"total\": len(events),",
    "        \"failed\": failed,",
    "        \"first_failure_cmd\": first_failure,",
    "        \"redacted_logs\": redacted_logs,",
    "    }",
    "```"
  ]
}
